IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa6-notification-of-changes.l4: the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 12 (Company secretaries), the cross-heading
-- "Notification of information about secretaries": ss 279G, 279H and 279I (lines 3646-3670 of ukpga-2006-46.txt).
-- Layer 1 of the part agent coa6: the law, objectively, from the text alone.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: as in coa6-private-and-public.l4. JUST TRUE is the text's yes; JUST FALSE the text's no in its own words
-- (an "if" that fails; a period the text fixes, outside it; a flat negative; a "must" not done); NOTHING "not covered" (a duty
-- limited by its own wording such as "of any change", a period still running, a point the text does not settle).
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
--
-- THE PERIOD. "within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which ..." counts the first day as day 1, so the last day
-- is the 13th day after the first (the first day plus 13): a notice given on the 14th day is in time, on the 15th it is not.
--
-- SEAMS (inputs, named for the section that answers; this module imports coa-core only):
--   s 12  whether the person is named in the statement of proposed officers as the proposed secretary or a proposed joint
--         secretary (a fact the person can state), ss 279G(4), 279I(1) and (2);
--   s 9   the day the application for the company's registration was delivered to the registrar (a date), s 279I(2);
--   ss 279J and 279K  what "the required information" is: coa6-required-information.l4 (this part), taken here as a plain fact
--         ("the notice contains a statement of the required information").

§ `Part 12 -- Company secretaries`

§§ `Notification of information about secretaries`

-- ---- s 279G: Duty to notify registrar of change in secretary or joint secretary --------------------------------------------

-- src:3648 | (1) A company must give notice to the registrar if a person—
-- src:3649 | (a) becomes the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of the company, or
-- src:3650 | (b) ceases to be the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of the company.
@ref s 279G(1) Duty to notify registrar of change in secretary or joint secretary: the two changes (src:3648-3650)
DECLARE `s 279G change in the secretaries` IS ONE OF
    `s 279G(1)(a) a person becomes the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of the company`
    `s 279G(1)(b) a person ceases to be the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of the company`
    `s 279G no such change`

-- (1) "A company must give notice to the registrar if a person (a) becomes ..., or (b) ceases ...", with the exception of (4):
-- "Subsection (1)(a) does not require a company, on its incorporation, to give notice in relation to a person named as the
-- proposed secretary or one of the proposed joint secretaries of the company in the statement under section 12."
-- src:3648 | (1) A company must give notice to the registrar if a person—
-- src:3649 | (a) becomes the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of the company, or
-- src:3650 | (b) ceases to be the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of the company.
-- src:3655 | (4) Subsection (1)(a) does not require a company, on its incorporation, to give notice in relation to a person named as the proposed secretary or one of the proposed joint secretaries of the company in the statement under section 12.
@ref s 279G(1) Duty to notify registrar of change in secretary or joint secretary (src:3648-3655)
GIVEN change IS A `s 279G change in the secretaries`
      `the person becomes the secretary or a joint secretary on the company's incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 12 the person is named in the statement as the proposed secretary or one of the proposed joint secretaries` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279G(1) the company must give notice to the registrar` MEANS
    CONSIDER change
    WHEN `s 279G(1)(a) a person becomes the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of the company` THEN
        IF `the person becomes the secretary or a joint secretary on the company's incorporation` AND `s 12 the person is named in the statement as the proposed secretary or one of the proposed joint secretaries`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1)(a) does not require a company, on its incorporation, to give notice in relation to a person named as the proposed secretary or one of the proposed joint secretaries of the company in the statement under section 12"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 279G(1)(b) a person ceases to be the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 279G no such change` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must give notice to the registrar if a person (a) becomes the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of the company, or (b) ceases to be"

-- src:3651 | (2) The notice must specify the date on which the person became or ceased to be the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of the company.
@ref s 279G(2) The notice must specify the date (src:3651)
GIVEN `the notice specifies the date on which the person became or ceased to be the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279G(2) the notice specifies the date` MEANS
    IF `the notice specifies the date on which the person became or ceased to be the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice must specify the date on which the person became or ceased to be the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of the company"

-- src:3652 | (3) A notice under subsection (1)(a) must contain—
-- src:3653 | (a) a statement of the required information about the secretary or joint secretary (see sections 279J and 279K), and
-- src:3654 | (b) a statement by the company that the person has consented to act in that capacity.
@ref s 279G(3) A notice under subsection (1)(a) must contain two statements (src:3652-3654)
GIVEN change IS A `s 279G change in the secretaries`
      `the notice contains a statement of the required information about the secretary or joint secretary (sections 279J and 279K)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice contains a statement by the company that the person has consented to act in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279G(3) the notice under subsection (1)(a) contains the statements required` MEANS
    CONSIDER change
    WHEN `s 279G(1)(a) a person becomes the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of the company` THEN
        IF `the notice contains a statement of the required information about the secretary or joint secretary (sections 279J and 279K)` AND `the notice contains a statement by the company that the person has consented to act in that capacity`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice under subsection (1)(a) must contain— (a) a statement of the required information about the secretary or joint secretary (see sections 279J and 279K), and (b) a statement by the company that the person has consented to act in that capacity"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A notice under subsection (1)(a)"

-- src:3656 | (5) A notice under this section must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the person becomes or ceases to be the secretary or a joint secretary.
@ref s 279G(5) The period of 14 days (src:3656)
`s 279G(5) the days in the period` MEANS 14

-- src:3656 | (5) A notice under this section must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the person becomes or ceases to be the secretary or a joint secretary.
@ref s 279G(5) The last day of the period (src:3656)
GIVEN `the day on which the person becomes or ceases to be the secretary or a joint secretary` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 279G(5) the last day of the period` MEANS
    `the day on which the person becomes or ceases to be the secretary or a joint secretary` PLUS (`s 279G(5) the days in the period` MINUS 1)

-- src:3656 | (5) A notice under this section must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the person becomes or ceases to be the secretary or a joint secretary.
@ref s 279G(5) The notice must be given within the period (src:3656)
GIVEN `the day on which the person becomes or ceases to be the secretary or a joint secretary` IS A DATE
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279G(5) the notice was given within the period` MEANS
    IF       `the day the notice was given` AT LEAST `the day on which the person becomes or ceases to be the secretary or a joint secretary`
         AND `the day the notice was given` AT MOST `s 279G(5) the last day of the period` `the day on which the person becomes or ceases to be the secretary or a joint secretary`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice under this section must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the person becomes or ceases to be the secretary or a joint secretary"

-- The notice as given, so that "fails to comply with section 279G" (s 279M(1)) can be decided.
-- src:3651 | (2) The notice must specify the date on which the person became or ceased to be the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of the company.
-- src:3652 | (3) A notice under subsection (1)(a) must contain—
-- src:3653 | (a) a statement of the required information about the secretary or joint secretary (see sections 279J and 279K), and
-- src:3654 | (b) a statement by the company that the person has consented to act in that capacity.
-- src:3655 | (4) Subsection (1)(a) does not require a company, on its incorporation, to give notice in relation to a person named as the proposed secretary or one of the proposed joint secretaries of the company in the statement under section 12.
-- src:3656 | (5) A notice under this section must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the person becomes or ceases to be the secretary or a joint secretary.
@ref s 279G(2)-(5) The notice as given (src:3651-3656)
DECLARE `s 279G notice given` HAS
    `s 279G the day the notice was given` IS A DATE
    `s 279G the notice specifies the date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 279G the notice contains a statement of the required information` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 279G the notice contains a statement of consent` IS A BOOLEAN

-- "Fails to comply with section 279G": the section required a notice and none was given in the period, or the notice given was
-- late or lacked what (2) and (3) require. JUST TRUE is a failure, JUST FALSE is no failure (the section did not require a
-- notice, or the notice given satisfies it), NOTHING is not yet decided (no notice yet while the period is still running).
-- src:3648 | (1) A company must give notice to the registrar if a person—
-- src:3649 | (a) becomes the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of the company, or
-- src:3650 | (b) ceases to be the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of the company.
-- src:3651 | (2) The notice must specify the date on which the person became or ceased to be the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of the company.
-- src:3652 | (3) A notice under subsection (1)(a) must contain—
-- src:3653 | (a) a statement of the required information about the secretary or joint secretary (see sections 279J and 279K), and
-- src:3654 | (b) a statement by the company that the person has consented to act in that capacity.
-- src:3655 | (4) Subsection (1)(a) does not require a company, on its incorporation, to give notice in relation to a person named as the proposed secretary or one of the proposed joint secretaries of the company in the statement under section 12.
-- src:3656 | (5) A notice under this section must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the person becomes or ceases to be the secretary or a joint secretary.
@ref s 279G Failure to comply with section 279G (src:3648-3656)
GIVEN change IS A `s 279G change in the secretaries`
      `the person becomes the secretary or a joint secretary on the company's incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 12 the person is named in the statement as the proposed secretary or one of the proposed joint secretaries` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the person becomes or ceases to be the secretary or a joint secretary` IS A DATE
      notice IS A MAYBE `s 279G notice given`
      `the day of the question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279G the company has failed to comply with section 279G` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 279G(1) the company must give notice to the registrar` change `the person becomes the secretary or a joint secretary on the company's incorporation` `s 12 the person is named in the statement as the proposed secretary or one of the proposed joint secretaries`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the section required no notice ("Subsection (1)(a) does not require a company, on its incorporation, to give notice"; "A company must give notice ... if")
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 279G(1) is not settled
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER notice
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            IF `the day of the question` AT MOST `s 279G(5) the last day of the period` `the day on which the person becomes or ceases to be the secretary or a joint secretary`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "within the period of 14 days" (the period has not ended)
            ELSE JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST n THEN
            IF       (`s 279G(5) the notice was given within the period` `the day on which the person becomes or ceases to be the secretary or a joint secretary` (n's `s 279G the day the notice was given`) EQUALS JUST TRUE)
                 AND n's `s 279G the notice specifies the date`
                 AND (    (change EQUALS `s 279G(1)(b) a person ceases to be the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of the company`)
                       OR (n's `s 279G the notice contains a statement of the required information` AND n's `s 279G the notice contains a statement of consent`))
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must give notice to the registrar", the notice being given in time and with what (2) and (3) require
            ELSE JUST TRUE

-- The duty as a regulative rule: the clock counts days from the first day of the period (time 0), so the last day is time 13.
-- src:3648 | (1) A company must give notice to the registrar if a person—
-- src:3649 | (a) becomes the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of the company, or
-- src:3650 | (b) ceases to be the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of the company.
-- src:3651 | (2) The notice must specify the date on which the person became or ceased to be the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of the company.
-- src:3652 | (3) A notice under subsection (1)(a) must contain—
-- src:3653 | (a) a statement of the required information about the secretary or joint secretary (see sections 279J and 279K), and
-- src:3654 | (b) a statement by the company that the person has consented to act in that capacity.
-- src:3655 | (4) Subsection (1)(a) does not require a company, on its incorporation, to give notice in relation to a person named as the proposed secretary or one of the proposed joint secretaries of the company in the statement under section 12.
-- src:3656 | (5) A notice under this section must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the person becomes or ceases to be the secretary or a joint secretary.
@ref s 279G(1) and (5) The duty (regulative) (src:3648-3656)
`s 279G(5) the number of days from the first day of the period to its last day` MEANS `s 279G(5) the days in the period` MINUS 1

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 279G(1) and (5) the company's duty as a regulative rule` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Company, Registrar, "give notice of the change in the secretaries (s 279G(1))"
    WITHIN `s 279G(5) the number of days from the first day of the period to its last day`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "notice was not given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day of the change (s 279G(5))"

-- ---- s 279H: Duty to notify registrar of changes of information -----------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3658 | (1) A company must give notice to the registrar of any change in the required information about the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of the company (see sections 279J and 279K).
@ref s 279H(1) Duty to notify registrar of changes of information (src:3658)
GIVEN `there is a change in the required information about the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279H(1) the company must give notice to the registrar of the change` MEANS
    IF `there is a change in the required information about the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company must give notice to the registrar of any change in the required information about the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of the company"

-- src:3659 | (2) The notice must specify the date on which the change occurred.
@ref s 279H(2) The notice must specify the date (src:3659)
GIVEN `the notice specifies the date on which the change occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279H(2) the notice specifies the date` MEANS
    IF `the notice specifies the date on which the change occurred`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice must specify the date on which the change occurred"

-- src:3660 | (3) A notice under this section must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the change occurs.
@ref s 279H(3) The period of 14 days (src:3660)
`s 279H(3) the days in the period` MEANS 14

-- src:3660 | (3) A notice under this section must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the change occurs.
@ref s 279H(3) The last day of the period (src:3660)
GIVEN `the day on which the change occurs` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 279H(3) the last day of the period` MEANS
    `the day on which the change occurs` PLUS (`s 279H(3) the days in the period` MINUS 1)

-- src:3660 | (3) A notice under this section must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the change occurs.
@ref s 279H(3) The notice must be given within the period (src:3660)
GIVEN `the day on which the change occurs` IS A DATE
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279H(3) the notice was given within the period` MEANS
    IF       `the day the notice was given` AT LEAST `the day on which the change occurs`
         AND `the day the notice was given` AT MOST `s 279H(3) the last day of the period` `the day on which the change occurs`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice under this section must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the change occurs"

-- src:3659 | (2) The notice must specify the date on which the change occurred.
-- src:3660 | (3) A notice under this section must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the change occurs.
@ref s 279H(2)-(3) The notice as given (src:3659-3660)
DECLARE `s 279H notice given` HAS
    `s 279H the day the notice was given` IS A DATE
    `s 279H the notice specifies the date` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:3658 | (1) A company must give notice to the registrar of any change in the required information about the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of the company (see sections 279J and 279K).
-- src:3659 | (2) The notice must specify the date on which the change occurred.
-- src:3660 | (3) A notice under this section must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the change occurs.
@ref s 279H Failure to comply with section 279H (src:3658-3660)
GIVEN `s 279H(1) the company must give notice to the registrar of the change` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the change occurs` IS A DATE
      notice IS A MAYBE `s 279H notice given`
      `the day of the question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279H the company has failed to comply with section 279H` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 279H(1) the company must give notice to the registrar of the change`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the section required no notice
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "of any change in the required information" (there is no such change)
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER notice
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            IF `the day of the question` AT MOST `s 279H(3) the last day of the period` `the day on which the change occurs`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "within the period of 14 days" (the period has not ended)
            ELSE JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST n THEN
            IF       (`s 279H(3) the notice was given within the period` `the day on which the change occurs` (n's `s 279H the day the notice was given`) EQUALS JUST TRUE)
                 AND n's `s 279H the notice specifies the date`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must give notice to the registrar of any change", given in time and specifying the date
            ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:3658 | (1) A company must give notice to the registrar of any change in the required information about the secretary or one of the joint secretaries of the company (see sections 279J and 279K).
-- src:3659 | (2) The notice must specify the date on which the change occurred.
-- src:3660 | (3) A notice under this section must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the change occurs.
@ref s 279H(1) and (3) The duty (regulative) (src:3658-3660)
`s 279H(3) the number of days from the first day of the period to its last day` MEANS `s 279H(3) the days in the period` MINUS 1

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 279H(1) and (3) the company's duty as a regulative rule` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Company, Registrar, "give notice of the change in the required information (s 279H(1))"
    WITHIN `s 279H(3) the number of days from the first day of the period to its last day`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "notice was not given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day the change occurs (s 279H(3))"

-- ---- s 279I: Notification of changes occurring before company's incorporation --------------------------------------------

-- (1): "if (a) a person named in the statement under section 12 as the proposed secretary of the company did not become the
-- secretary on its incorporation, or (b) a person named ... as one of the proposed joint secretaries ... did not become one of the
-- joint secretaries on its incorporation". (The text prints "become did not become" in (b); finding F-279I-1b in NOTES.md.)
-- src:3662 | (1) A company must give notice to the registrar if—
-- src:3663 | (a) a person named in the statement under section 12 as the proposed secretary of the company did not become the secretary on its incorporation, or
-- src:3664 | (b) a person named in the statement under section 12 as one of the proposed joint secretaries of the company become did not become one of the joint secretaries on its incorporation.
@ref s 279I(1) Notification of changes occurring before incorporation: a proposed secretary who did not become secretary (src:3662-3664)
GIVEN `s 12 the person is named in the statement as the proposed secretary or as one of the proposed joint secretaries of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person did not become the secretary or one of the joint secretaries on the company's incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279I(1) the company must give notice to the registrar that a proposed secretary did not become the secretary` MEANS
    IF       `s 12 the person is named in the statement as the proposed secretary or as one of the proposed joint secretaries of the company`
         AND `the person did not become the secretary or one of the joint secretaries on the company's incorporation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must give notice to the registrar if— (a) a person named in the statement under section 12 as the proposed secretary of the company did not become the secretary on its incorporation"

-- (2) and (3): a change in the required information about a proposed secretary "that occurred (a) after the application for the
-- company's registration under section 9 was delivered to the registrar, but (b) before the company was incorporated"; not
-- required "in respect of a person if it gives notice under subsection (1) in respect of the person".
-- src:3665 | (2) A company must give notice to the registrar of any change in the required information about a proposed secretary, or one of the proposed joint secretaries, that occurred—
-- src:3666 | (a) after the application for the company’s registration under section 9 was delivered to the registrar, but
-- src:3667 | (b) before the company was incorporated.
-- src:3668 | (3) But a company is not required to give notice under subsection (2) in respect of a person if it gives notice under subsection (1) in respect of the person.
@ref s 279I(2) Notification of changes occurring before incorporation: a change in the required information (src:3665-3668)
GIVEN `the person is a proposed secretary or one of the proposed joint secretaries of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there was a change in the required information about the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the change occurred` IS A DATE
      `s 9 the day the application for the company's registration was delivered to the registrar` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the company was incorporated` IS A DATE
      `the company gives notice under subsection (1) in respect of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279I(2) the company must give notice to the registrar of the change in the required information` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the person is a proposed secretary or one of the proposed joint secretaries of the company`)) OR (NOT (`there was a change in the required information about the person`))
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any change in the required information about a proposed secretary, or one of the proposed joint secretaries"
    ELSE IF `the company gives notice under subsection (1) in respect of the person`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a company is not required to give notice under subsection (2) in respect of a person if it gives notice under subsection (1) in respect of the person"
         ELSE IF       (`the day on which the change occurred` GREATER THAN `s 9 the day the application for the company's registration was delivered to the registrar`)
                   AND (`the day on which the change occurred` LESS THAN `the day on which the company was incorporated`)
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE IF       (`the day on which the change occurred` LESS THAN `s 9 the day the application for the company's registration was delivered to the registrar`)
                         OR (`the day on which the change occurred` GREATER THAN `the day on which the company was incorporated`)
                   THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that occurred (a) after the application for the company’s registration under section 9 was delivered to the registrar, but (b) before the company was incorporated"
                   ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the change fell on the day the application was delivered or on the day of incorporation, and the text compares events, not days

-- src:3669 | (4) A notice under subsection (2) must specify the date on which the change occurred.
@ref s 279I(4) A notice under subsection (2) must specify the date (src:3669)
GIVEN `the notice specifies the date on which the change occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279I(4) the notice under subsection (2) specifies the date` MEANS
    IF `the notice specifies the date on which the change occurred`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice under subsection (2) must specify the date on which the change occurred"

-- src:3670 | (5) A notice under this section must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the company was incorporated.
@ref s 279I(5) The period of 14 days (src:3670)
`s 279I(5) the days in the period` MEANS 14

-- src:3670 | (5) A notice under this section must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the company was incorporated.
@ref s 279I(5) The last day of the period (src:3670)
GIVEN `the day on which the company was incorporated` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 279I(5) the last day of the period` MEANS
    `the day on which the company was incorporated` PLUS (`s 279I(5) the days in the period` MINUS 1)

-- src:3670 | (5) A notice under this section must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the company was incorporated.
@ref s 279I(5) The notice must be given within the period (src:3670)
GIVEN `the day on which the company was incorporated` IS A DATE
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279I(5) the notice was given within the period` MEANS
    IF       `the day the notice was given` AT LEAST `the day on which the company was incorporated`
         AND `the day the notice was given` AT MOST `s 279I(5) the last day of the period` `the day on which the company was incorporated`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice under this section must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the company was incorporated"

-- src:3669 | (4) A notice under subsection (2) must specify the date on which the change occurred.
-- src:3670 | (5) A notice under this section must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the company was incorporated.
@ref s 279I(4)-(5) The notice as given (src:3669-3670)
DECLARE `s 279I notice given` HAS
    `s 279I the day the notice was given` IS A DATE
    `s 279I the notice specifies the date on which the change occurred` IS A BOOLEAN

-- "Fails to comply with section 279I": the answers of (1) and (2) say whether a notice was required; the notice given is judged by
-- (4) (the date, where (2) applies) and (5) (the period).
-- src:3662 | (1) A company must give notice to the registrar if—
-- src:3663 | (a) a person named in the statement under section 12 as the proposed secretary of the company did not become the secretary on its incorporation, or
-- src:3664 | (b) a person named in the statement under section 12 as one of the proposed joint secretaries of the company become did not become one of the joint secretaries on its incorporation.
-- src:3665 | (2) A company must give notice to the registrar of any change in the required information about a proposed secretary, or one of the proposed joint secretaries, that occurred—
-- src:3666 | (a) after the application for the company’s registration under section 9 was delivered to the registrar, but
-- src:3667 | (b) before the company was incorporated.
-- src:3668 | (3) But a company is not required to give notice under subsection (2) in respect of a person if it gives notice under subsection (1) in respect of the person.
-- src:3669 | (4) A notice under subsection (2) must specify the date on which the change occurred.
-- src:3670 | (5) A notice under this section must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the company was incorporated.
@ref s 279I Failure to comply with section 279I (src:3662-3670)
GIVEN `s 279I(1) the company must give notice to the registrar that a proposed secretary did not become the secretary` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 279I(2) the company must give notice to the registrar of the change in the required information` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the company was incorporated` IS A DATE
      notice IS A MAYBE `s 279I notice given`
      `the day of the question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279I the company has failed to comply with section 279I` MEANS
    IF       (`s 279I(1) the company must give notice to the registrar that a proposed secretary did not become the secretary` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
         OR  (`s 279I(2) the company must give notice to the registrar of the change in the required information` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN CONSIDER notice
         WHEN NOTHING THEN
             IF `the day of the question` AT MOST `s 279I(5) the last day of the period` `the day on which the company was incorporated`
             THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "within the period of 14 days" (the period has not ended)
             ELSE JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST n THEN
             IF       (`s 279I(5) the notice was given within the period` `the day on which the company was incorporated` (n's `s 279I the day the notice was given`) EQUALS JUST TRUE)
                  AND (    (NOT (`s 279I(2) the company must give notice to the registrar of the change in the required information` EQUALS JUST TRUE))
                        OR n's `s 279I the notice specifies the date on which the change occurred`)
             THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must give notice to the registrar", given within the period and (under (2)) specifying the date
             ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF       (`s 279I(1) the company must give notice to the registrar that a proposed secretary did not become the secretary` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
              AND (`s 279I(2) the company must give notice to the registrar of the change in the required information` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): neither (1) nor (2) required a notice
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 279I(1) or (2) is not settled

-- src:3662 | (1) A company must give notice to the registrar if—
-- src:3663 | (a) a person named in the statement under section 12 as the proposed secretary of the company did not become the secretary on its incorporation, or
-- src:3664 | (b) a person named in the statement under section 12 as one of the proposed joint secretaries of the company become did not become one of the joint secretaries on its incorporation.
-- src:3665 | (2) A company must give notice to the registrar of any change in the required information about a proposed secretary, or one of the proposed joint secretaries, that occurred—
-- src:3666 | (a) after the application for the company’s registration under section 9 was delivered to the registrar, but
-- src:3667 | (b) before the company was incorporated.
-- src:3668 | (3) But a company is not required to give notice under subsection (2) in respect of a person if it gives notice under subsection (1) in respect of the person.
-- src:3669 | (4) A notice under subsection (2) must specify the date on which the change occurred.
-- src:3670 | (5) A notice under this section must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the company was incorporated.
@ref s 279I(1)-(5) The duty (regulative) (src:3662-3670)
`s 279I(5) the number of days from the first day of the period to its last day` MEANS `s 279I(5) the days in the period` MINUS 1

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 279I(1), (2) and (5) the company's duty as a regulative rule` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Company, Registrar, "give notice of the change occurring before incorporation (s 279I(1) or (2))"
    WITHIN `s 279I(5) the number of days from the first day of the period to its last day`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "notice was not given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day the company was incorporated (s 279I(5))"
